config IEC60730B_TEST_WDOG_DTCM_NOINIT
    bool "Place watchdog counter variable in DTCM noinit section"
    depends on IEC60730B_TEST_WDOG
    select CODE_DATA_RELOCATION
    default y if (NXP_IMX_EXTERNAL_SDRAM || NXP_IMX_EXTERNAL_HYPERRAM) && DT_HAS_NXP_IMX_DTCM_ENABLED
    help
      On boards where zephyr,sram is external volatile memory (SDRAM,
      HyperRAM, PSRAM), the memory controller is re-initialised on every
      reset, destroying all RAM contents — including __noinit variables.
      This defeats the watchdog test's cross-reset counter persistence.
      When enabled, noinit data is relocated to
      DTCM_NOINIT (on-chip Data TCM), which retains
      its contents across watchdog-triggered resets.

